Now sound.js: dedupe the repeated `const ctx = this.ensure(); if (!ctx) return; const t = ctx.currentTime` boilerplate with a `_seq(notes)` helper.

Current methods: powerup, trumpRelease, counterKill, dungeonClear, collect, brew, gameOver all have that pattern.

Let me add:
```js
  // 序列音：notes = [[freq, dur, type, vol, slideTo?], ...]
  _seq(notes) {
    const ctx = this.ensure()
    if (!ctx) return
    const t0 = ctx.currentTime
    let at = 0
    for (const [freq, dur, type, vol, slideTo] of notes) {
      this._scheduleTone(t0 + at, freq, dur, type, vol, slideTo)
      at += dur
    }
  }
```
Hmm the existing code uses explicit offsets not cumulative durations. E.g. powerup: t, t+0.08 with dur 0.09/0.12. Cumulative would be t, t+0.09. Close enough but changes sound slightly. I'd rather keep explicit offsets.

Let me use `[[at, freq, dur, type, vol], ...]` with explicit at.

```js
  _seq(notes) {
    const ctx = this.ensure()
    if (!ctx) return
    const t0 = ctx.currentTime
    for (let i = 0; i < notes.length; i++) {
      const n = notes[i]
      this._scheduleTone(t0 + n[0], n[1], n[2], n[3], n[4])
    }
  }
```

