}
```
Getters in an object literal are ES5-compatible? `get entered(){}` in object literal is ES5. Douyin supports ES6 anyway (es6: true in config). Fine.

Actually simpler: export functions + a mutable state object. Let me keep `launch` with getters — cleaner API for game.js:

```js
